e'), reroute_migrated_plans (today excludes any create-bearing plan), and applier._apply_one's legacy create_one loop — and state how the selector guarantees a create is dispatched by exactly one of the coordinator route or the legacy loop (never both).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["batch_dispatch.py route_for: 'route override not permitted for non-cutover family' + create is not in NON_CREATE_FAMILIES, so create currently stays on LEGACY_ROUTE and cannot be routed to coordinator","batch_dispatch.py reroute_migrated_plans: migrated iff 'all(route_for(m.action.value) == COORDINATOR_ROUTE ...)', so a create plan is excluded and falls through to the legacy loop","applier.py:659-676: reroute_migrated_plans runs first, then the remaining mutations (which today include every create) are dispatched by _apply_one via the legacy create_one path","Plan names no artifact for the 'internal family rollback selector' or the legacy create consumer it must fence off"],"finding":"The create-family cutover changes live consumers outside the create-coordinator/containment modules that the plan does not enumerate: batch_dispatch.route_for currently rejects 'create' (raises ValueError for a create override), reroute_migrated_plans excludes any plan containing a create action, and applier._apply_one still dispatches create via the legacy create_one loop. Making coordinated create authoritative behind the selector requires updating all three in lockstep, or a create can be dispatched by BOTH the legacy loop and the coordinator route (the exact dual-send AC6 forbids).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0b407c5e1029a6a0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 / Acceptance Criteria line 'Create has one coordinator route and one internal legacy rollback value with no dual-send'","norm_id":"n5348e90c23f1c0c7","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Cutover flips the create default to coordinator but the applier legacy create loop / reroute create-exclusion is not updated, so a create fires on both routes (dual remote issue)","route_for's create-reject guard is left in place, so the selector cannot actually route create and the cutover silently no-ops onto legacy"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a step naming the create route selector (analogous to route_for/NON_CREATE_FAMILIES) and its three touched consumers — route_for's create-reject guard, reroute_migrated_plans' create exclusion, and applier's legacy create_one dispatch — with an explicit no-dual-send assertion that the selected route removes the create mutation from the other path.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"find